  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Public Procurement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Bank has conducted a Country Procurement Assessment Review in Moldova in 2010 which resulted in a number of recommendations. The Public Procurement Agency (PPA) is in charge of the Public Procurement agenda and has been working with various stakeholders to strengthen the system among others by following the recommendations of the Bank&apos;s CPAR. While a major part of capacity building and other efforts has been addressed by a twinning arrangement with Romania under the leadership of the EU, there are some important areas left which the PPA wants to address and is seeking funding for.  To this end, the Minister of Finance has applied for an IDF Grant in the amount of USD 500,000 to further engage in the design and implementation of the e-Procurement system, support the standardization of procurement documents, and fund capacity building activities. All these components are considered as high priority by the Government and the Bank in reforming the public procurement system with focus on innovation, standardization, and capacity development. TF012004</narrative>
  </description>
